# s16_os_cross.tkr — §16 `#os` cross-emit: an `#os`-split const family AND an `#os`-split function
# family both defer the OS axis to the emitted C `#if`, so the one `teko.c` carries the Linux+macOS+
# Windows arms. On a Linux host the `#if defined(__linux__)` arms select OS_CODE = 42 and os_tag() = 42.

Feature: §16 #os cross-emit — const and function OS arms ladder into one teko.c

  Scenario: linux_os_ladder_selects_42 — on Linux the #if ladder selects the Linux arm, os_tag() = 42
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 42
